[{:db/id "q-338763/field-1/581509c1a593b3ff4f4c3c9fd65f6549ed3b67bbd6bc1abd05a3856dbb76597f" :answer/id #uuid "d5de5934-d762-554e-9bc6-54960f23fa75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "205" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338763/field-1/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" :answer/id #uuid "b9a344ae-c1a6-5f5f-a096-a66d926f1d2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338763/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "deb06272-2dd7-53c0-a9ac-40dfef3ec089" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-338763/field-1/581509c1a593b3ff4f4c3c9fd65f6549ed3b67bbd6bc1abd05a3856dbb76597f" :answer-field/choices ["q-338763/field-1/581509c1a593b3ff4f4c3c9fd65f6549ed3b67bbd6bc1abd05a3856dbb76597f" "q-338763/field-1/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338763/field-2/4cd7e68ca4dc7a3ea725571a6860c3e1e4090ced7cff84ef33c048f865979a66" :answer/id #uuid "737ee07b-e384-58c6-b1e3-24519c6cc192" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "335" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338763/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "712f34e8-a73a-51dc-8e5e-7f215f9c90ce" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-338763/field-2/4cd7e68ca4dc7a3ea725571a6860c3e1e4090ced7cff84ef33c048f865979a66" :answer-field/choices ["q-338763/field-2/4cd7e68ca4dc7a3ea725571a6860c3e1e4090ced7cff84ef33c048f865979a66"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338763" :question/id #uuid "190ea00f-cebd-5a8c-93af-4aa5ffc827ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-338763" :question/problem "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions to the equation $-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=7+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ are\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,x≈$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =7+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x \\\\ -3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =7 \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =-\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{3}{7}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{3}{7})=(-25.376\\,933…)^{∘}≈-{25.377}^{∘}\n$$\n\nThis value is outside the required domain. To get a value inside the range, we add ${360}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-{25.377}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={334.623}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSo,  our first solution is ${x}_{1}={334.623}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={25.377}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={25.377}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/assets/2358d2c829f52ba8727afc10a609f923ca441bb55dc398cda78c619454f6eac5.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{25.377}^{∘} \\\\  & ={205.377}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx≈{205}^{∘},\\,x≈{335}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/requires-calculator true :question/answer-fields ["q-338763/field-1" "q-338763/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9ccf6b5-e087-5f7b-88e3-3767efbdcc26"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338763"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-279424/field-1/ca13211c2d7f0281a20bb4814e5a56a668520d0ac82b242179051cd495f78eab" :answer/id #uuid "836392e0