"38" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279424/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "709c9dfd-3c35-5887-8504-55c653b794b3" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279424/field-4/2671fdc3a44bd3421ded09be4e881743067a96eb4e584e442a30f737593eae71" :answer-field/choices ["q-279424/field-4/2671fdc3a44bd3421ded09be4e881743067a96eb4e584e442a30f737593eae71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279424" :question/id #uuid "2b2c5b2b-c1cc-5494-8426-31e14143c9c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-279424" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $H=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ Find ${H}^{3}.$\n\n| ${H}^{3}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, to find ${H}^{2},$ we multiply $H$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}^{2} & =H\\cdot H \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}23 & -18 \\\\ 9 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${H}^{3}={H}^{2}\\cdot H,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}^{3} & ={H}^{2}\\cdot H \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}23 & -18 \\\\ 9 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}97 & -118 \\\\ 59 & 38\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279424/field-1" "q-279424/field-2" "q-279424/field-3" "q-279424/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e970fe-cff8-50e3-9b94-67ad97b03da7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279424"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342050/field-1/7385d1fc9f0efddcbb9b82384fb5143cec1a75f5c34d8e04e10208c76c1c1e3c" :answer/id #uuid "d73c84b8-1e28-5cae-a18d-1cf0d787882d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+11}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342050/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "86959dbd-2403-5dd4-b220-c2a739f4834b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342050/field-1/7385d1fc9f0efddcbb9b82384fb5143cec1a75f5c34d8e04e10208c76c1c1e3c" :answer-field/choices ["q-342050/field-1/7385d1fc9f0efddcbb9b82384fb5143cec1a75f5c34d8e04e10208c76c1c1e3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342050" :question/id #uuid "4c4511dd-c475-5538-9512-79a65c337158" :question/math-academy-id "q-342050" :question/problem "Given a curve $x=-\\frac{5}{y}+{y}^{2},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-4,1)?$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{5}{y}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-5{y}^{-1}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-5(-{y}^{-2})+2y \\\\  & =2y+5{y}^{-2} \\\\  & =2y+\\frac{5}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{y}^{3}+5}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2{y}^{3}+5}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-4,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-4,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2(1)^{3}+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (x-(-4)) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{7}x+\\frac{4}{7}+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{7}x+\\frac{11}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342050/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ff302ba-5a3f-599b-b038-7417af1dca71"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342050"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-135990/selection/9a83de236a8a69aef4593f469a2c1d7503050160132466135a2cb3a8a9bf2514" :answer/id #uuid "c31ff4a0-c2f7-5757-8408-08f8e7334d82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+25t+450{t}^{2}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135990/selection/5355fe8bf0caa37dedf37f8dbeaba78f037ff8a3ff30fcac8ccfdff1bec3b1ca" :answer/id #uuid "1c8b72aa-d6c6-5592-b992-b44117372f84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-35t+500{t}^{2}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135990/selection/41d3e9b790a6342fd27b44ccd2f3e4262b8a683d1ebaa8c3e2f2b15f7cce53a9" :answer/id #uuid "24382456-110a-5c22-ac1b-99c764eaa883" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-21t+550{t}^{2}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135990/selection/4f2ea174bedcfb9e04087c0e5616ac58254399ea909853917682e95b77cdff9e" :answer/id #uuid "2b7405ef-180c-5e34-88bd-22fab1e2a45b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-35t+525{t}^{2}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135990/selection/c16cfaaf4c4b4d5cda3d6ead2228dd7ad30de20106cd20ef3e3659ca91d620bf" :answer/id #uuid "dcea0204-2495-5161-a1c4-2c49ce230c3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+35t+485{t}^{2}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135990/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "454c71e5-cccf-58a6-90ef-e67c5530faf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-135990/selection/4f2ea174bedcfb9e04087c0e5616ac58254399ea909853917682e95b77cdff9e" :answer-field/choices ["q-135990/selection/9a83de236a8a69aef4593f469a2c1d7503050160132466135a2cb3a8a9bf2514" "q-135990/selection/5355fe8bf0caa37dedf37f8dbeaba78f037ff8a3ff30fcac8ccfdff1bec3b1ca" "q-135990/selection/41d3e9b790a6342fd27b44ccd2f3e4262b8a683d1ebaa8c3e2f2b15f7cce53a9" "q-135990/selection/4f2ea174bedcfb9e04087c0e5616ac58254399ea909853917682e95b77cdff9e" "q-135990/selection/c16cfaaf4c4b4d5cda3d6ead2228dd7ad30de20106cd20ef3e3659ca91d620bf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-135990" :question/id #uuid "93e6b933-e61e-5a9a-86f8-80581468e410" :question/math-academy-id "q-135990" :question/problem "${(1-5t)}^{7}=$" :question/worked-solution "The first three terms of the binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ are given by\n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+⋯.\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=-5t$ and $n=7$ into the above formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1-5t)}^{7} & =1+7\\cdot (-5t)+\\frac{7(7-1)}{2!}\\cdot (-5t)^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =1-35t+\\frac{7\\cdot 6}{2}\\cdot 25{t}^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =1-35t+21\\cdot 25{t}^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =1-35t+525{t}^{2}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-135990/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f3ba60a-8c09-563f-ae02-8183bb55e359"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-135990"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
